  "implemented_policy": [
    "Use the tuned Smart scorer as the base policy instead of the legacy inverted hand-value function.",
    "Simulate removal of exactly one physical card, including duplicated Jacks and Jokers.",
    "During a live penalty, consider only cards of the active penalty rank.",
    "Choose a Jack suit from the remaining own-hand suit histogram.",
    "Pass rather than play an effect card as the final card, and preserve the sole ordinary finisher in small hands.",
    "Save Jack and Joker when they are the only early exits.",
    "On ordinary two-player turns, combine remaining suit concentration with dashboard-derived rank pressure; use the threat table only when the opponent has exactly one card.",
    "Keep the prior Smart-based selection path for multiplayer and active-penalty turns.",
    "Keep canonical and batched implementations behaviorally identical and use only own-hand plus public state."
  ],
